_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":68.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.0022553616027125925,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":97.2,"_gate_piotroski":3,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":33.3,"_gate_spread":0.0026915704747482866,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":1.3,"_gate_roic_consistency":0.5145600515173908,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":14.2,"_gate_incr_roic":0.014886139670343789,"_gp_incr_roic":false,"_score_incr_roic":21.6,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.04179199561449626,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":19.4,"_gate_pool_share":0.009841930902155793,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":43.9,"_gate_rev_durability":0.005264233536097507,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":27.6,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.004785873559679385,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":45.2,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03659077992041726,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":51.8,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.03685972697746742,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":96.1,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0017621162592137724,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":97.1,"_gate_insider_own":0.01343,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":9.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Avnet, Inc., engages in the distribution of electronic component technology in the Americas, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, and Asia/Pacific. The company operates through two segments, Electronic Components and Farnell. It markets, sells, and distributes semiconductors; interconnect, passive, and electromechanical components; and other integrated and embedded components from electronic component manufacturers. The company also offers design support that provides engineers with technical design solutions; engineering and technical resources to support product design, bill of materials development, and technical education and training; and supply chain solutions which provides support, warehousing, and logistics services to original equipment manufacturers, electronic manufacturing service providers, and electronic component manufacturers. In addition, it provides embedded solutions, such as technical design, integration, and assembly of embedded products, systems, and solutions, as well as embedded display solutions comprising touch and passive displays; and develops and produces standard board and industrial subsystems, and application-specific devices that enable it to produce systems tailored to specific customer requirements. The company serves various markets, such as engineering, product prototyping, integration, and other value-added services in the medical, telecommunications, industrial, and digital editing. Further, it distributes kits, tools, and electronic and industrial automation components, as well as test and measurement products to engineers and entrepreneurs. The company was founded in 1921 and is headquartered in Tempe, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Philip R. Gallagher | CEO, President of Electronic Components, Member of Executive Board & Director | Age 64 | Compensation: $4.0M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 15K people. Revenue per employee of $1.8M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Avnet, Inc. is a mid-cap technology business with a $6.9B market cap on $27.6B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +1% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically, and 12% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $354M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.8\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and thin 2.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.1\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 121% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.2128146600384295},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Gross margin trails most Technology peers \u2014 competitors appear to have the pricing hand","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 48% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","13 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Avnet (AVT) Stock Still Looks Reasonable On Its 147% Run","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/avnet-avt-stock-still-looks-181018116.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794507018.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.869,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Is Strong Earnings Guidance Altering The Investment Case For Avnet (AVT)?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-avt/avnet/news/is-strong-earnings-guidance-altering-the-investment-case-for-3","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794483140.405,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.844,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Is Avnet (AVT) A Bargain After Strong Earnings And Fresh Guidance?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/tech/nasdaq-avt/avnet/news/is-avnet-avt-a-bargain-after-strong-earnings-and-fresh-guida","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794388852.03,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Analyzing Avnet (AVT) and Its Peers","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/analyzing-avnet-avt-and-its-peers.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794236327.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Why Avnet (AVT) International Revenue Trends Deserve Your At